From: Audrey Tang <au@civic.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dts): t8132: correct SEP mailbox IRQ roles

Patch 0004 copied the SEP mailbox interrupts in ADT order, which is not
the Linux role order. As patch 0015 found for the ANS mailbox, the line
in the recv-not-empty slot (391) is the one asserted while the receive
FIFO is empty. The ASC v4 mailbox has no IRQ acknowledge, so starting the
SEP channel makes the receive handler poll an empty FIFO forever and the
machine freezes.

On a J715, loading a SEP driver froze the machine at mailbox start every
time with the ADT order. With the roles below the same load starts the
channel, the SEP answers and recv-not-empty (392) counts its replies.
The send pair is exchanged to match, as in patch 0015.

The SoC include affects every T8132 board; hardware validation is J715
only. The SEP node itself stays disabled.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -592,10 +592,10 @@ sep_mbox: mbox@3aa608000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-asc-mailbox", "apple,asc-mailbox-v4";
 			reg = <0x3 0xaa608000 0x0 0x4000>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
-			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 390 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			             <AIC_IRQ 389 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			             <AIC_IRQ 392 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			             <AIC_IRQ 391 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 389 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			             <AIC_IRQ 390 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			             <AIC_IRQ 391 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			             <AIC_IRQ 392 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			interrupt-names = "send-empty", "send-not-empty",
 			                  "recv-empty", "recv-not-empty";
 			#mbox-cells = <0>;
